 EMPIRE CODE PARAMETRIZATION                                      2637 1451
 ---------------------------                                      2637 1451
                                                                  2637 1451
  Nuclear reaction model code EMPIRE-3.2.3 Malta                  2637 1451
  (SVN rev.  4977; source rev.  4977)                             2637 1451
 by M.W.Herman et al [EMP,EMP-man].                               2637 1451
                                                                  2637 1451
 EMPIRE dimensions (dimension.h):                                 2637 1451
  NDNUC= 160  NDEXCLUS= 50  NDEX= 241  NDLW= 100                  2637 1451
  LEVCC= 40  NDLV= 40  NDBR= 40  NDMSCS= 4                        2637 1451
                                                                  2637 1451
 The following EMPIRE-code modules and features were used in      2637 1451
 the current evaluation:                                          2637 1451
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 2637 1451
   coupled-channels code ECIS06 by J. Raynal                      2637 1451
 - Soft-rotator deformed Optical Model including                  2637 1451
   coupled-channels code OPTMAN by E.Soukhovitskii                2637 1451
   and coworkers                                                  2637 1451
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    2637 1451
   width fluctuation correction, and the                          2637 1451
   optical model for fission with partial damping                 2637 1451
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      2637 1451
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 2637 1451
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                2637 1451
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   2637 1451
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                2637 1451
   discrete transitions                                           2637 1451
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL library [RIPL]                2637 1451
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                2637 1451
   level density, discrete levels,                                2637 1451
   and gamma strength functions based on the RIPL                 2637 1451
   library [RIPL]                                                 2637 1451
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              2637 1451
   EXFOR library                                                  2637 1451
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A.Trkov)                     2637 1451
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 2637 1451
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                2637 1451
   PrePro codes by D. Cullen                                      2637 1451
 - ENDF checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                   2637 1451
                                                                  2637 1451
                      EMPIRE options                              2637 1451
                      --------------                              2637 1451
 Following options and deviations from the default values of      2637 1451
 the parameters were employed in the EMPIRE calculations:         2637 1451
                                                                  2637 1451
 - CC calculations using soft-rotor omp for the incident channel. 2637 1451
 - CN decay and Direct cross sections added incoherently.         2637 1451
 - Traditional Hauser-Feschbach Tlj_{CC}(E)=Tlj_{GS}(E-Egs).      2637 1451
 - HRTW width fluctuation correction calculated  up to 12.1 MeV.  2637 1451
 - Tlj coupling for the top CN bin  up to incident  9.90 MeV.     2637 1451
 - CN anisotropy calculated using Blatt-Biedenharn coefficients.  2637 1451
 - Coupled Channels Method used for Tl calcul. in outgoing ch.    2637 1451
 - Discrete levels were taken from the RIPL-3+                    2637 1451
    library based on the 2015 version of ENSDF.                   2637 1451
 - Gamma-transition multipolarity set to 2.                       2637 1451
 - GDR parameters taken from RIPL/Exp.data+Plujko systematics.    2637 1451
 - E1 strength function set to RIPL MLO1                          2637 1451
 - Gilbert-Cameron (EMPIRE 2.18) level densities.                 2637 1451
 - Preequilibrium mechanism treated in terms of the exciton model 2637 1451
    with the Iwamoto-Harada model for emission of clusters, and   2637 1451
    Kalbach systematics angular distributions (see RIPL-1)        2637 1451
                                                                  2637 1451
 Mean free path parameter in PCROSS set to  1.9 (Recomm:~1.5)     2637 1451
 PE emission width of ejectile 0 from  59Fe multiplied by  5.500  2637 1451
                                                                  2637 1451
